      <h2>Gold Mining Equipment for South America</h2>
      <p>South America is one of the world's most active alluvial gold mining regions, with major small- and medium-scale production across the Amazon Basin, the Guiana Shield, and the Andean foothills. Our wash plants are container-ready for shipping to Brazilian, Peruvian, Colombian, Guyanese, and Surinamese ports, and engineered for the tropical heat, heavy clay, and remote-camp conditions miners face in the region.</p>
      <h3>Why South American Miners Choose Us</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Container-ready for shipping into Santos, Manaus, Callao, Buenaventura, Georgetown, and Paramaribo</li>
        <li>Mercury-free — supports Minamata Convention compliance across the region</li>
        <li>Built for tropical clay, lateritic, and weathered greenstone alluvials</li>
        <li>Handles rainforest humidity, monsoon seasons, and remote river-camp conditions</li>
        <li>Simple operation suited to ASM and medium-scale crews</li>
        <li>30-minute setup means more productive hours per day on remote sites</li>
      </ul>
      <p>From the Tapajós and Madeira alluvials of the Brazilian Amazon to the Madre de Dios placers of Peru and the Guiana Shield deposits of Guyana and Suriname, our equipment is engineered for the realities of South American gold mining. <a href="/contact/">Contact us for regional pricing and shipping quotes</a>.</p>
